.TH mnnn-net 1  "mnnn-net 2.14.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-net \- The network: run a node, exchange keys with other nodes, share data with them, search across them and entrust them with dark shards. On with the TUI by default; nothing is shared until you ask
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn net\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
The network: run a node, exchange keys with other nodes, share data with them, search across them and entrust them with dark shards. On with the TUI by default; nothing is shared until you ask
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
The node starts with the TUI (turn that off with `mnnn net config \-\-autostart off`) or with
`mnnn net start`; other commands bring up a short\-lived node with the same identity when they
need to talk. Nothing is shared until you `share` it, and only with nodes you are connected to.
.PP
Connecting exchanges keys automatically. A node that knows you (or that you both asked)
connects at once; otherwise its owner sees a request to accept or decline. Keys are pinned to
the node on first contact, and you are warned if another node uses a known name. The token and
short\-code commands are still there, under `mnnn net exchange` (advanced).
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn net start \-\-for 3600
  mnnn net connect /ip4/192.0.2.7/tcp/4741/p2p/12D3Koo… \-\-label ben
  mnnn net invite                       # a link; they run `mnnn net connect LINK`
  mnnn net requests
  mnnn net accept ben
  mnnn net share journal "field notes" \-\-with ben
  mnnn net search \-\-journals \-\-query comet
  mnnn net fetch ben "field notes" \-\-import
  mnnn net shard entrust \-\-to ben \-\-to cleo \-\-to dev \-\-threshold 2
  mnnn net shard restore \-\-backup net\-backup.age \-\-recover
.PP
See `mnnn help network`, `mnnn help key\-exchanges` and `mnnn help dark\-shards`.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-net\-start(1)
Run this node in the foreground until Ctrl\-C (or \-\-for SECS, or `mnnn net stop`)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-stop(1)
Ask a node started with `mnnn net start` to stop
.TP
mnnn\-net\-status(1)
This node: identity, addresses, connections, NAT, relays
.TP
mnnn\-net\-peers(1)
Peers seen or known
.TP
mnnn\-net\-connect(1)
Connect to a node (`…/p2p/ID`, a peer id, a known name or an invite link): keys are exchanged automatically; a node that does not know you yet asks its owner first
.TP
mnnn\-net\-invite(1)
Make an invite link for another node: when they use it (`mnnn net connect LINK`, or paste it in the TUI), the two nodes connect. It holds no secret and expires in 7 days
.TP
mnnn\-net\-requests(1)
Requests waiting for you: nodes that want to connect, apply or invite you
.TP
mnnn\-net\-accept(1)
Accept a request (its id or the node\*(Aqs name)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-decline(1)
Decline a request (its id or the node\*(Aqs name)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-disconnect(1)
End the connection with a node: keys are erased on both sides
.TP
mnnn\-net\-forget(1)
Forget a known peer (exchanges with it are kept)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-relay(1)
Relays
.TP
mnnn\-net\-config(1)
Show or change network settings
.TP
mnnn\-net\-share(1)
Share an item: model, search, journal, project, report or code
.TP
mnnn\-net\-unshare(1)
Stop sharing an item (everywhere, or with \-\-with)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-shared(1)
What this node shares, and with whom
.TP
mnnn\-net\-list(1)
What a peer shares with us (all peers with an exchange when none is given)
.TP
mnnn\-net\-fetch(1)
Fetch an item a peer shares
.TP
mnnn\-net\-search(1)
Search here and on every peer that shares with you; results say where they came from
.TP
mnnn\-net\-shard(1)
Dark shards: the master key split among peers you exchanged keys with
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
